  "content": {
    "text": "Tech Stocks\nMicron suffers record market-cap wipeout as Broadcom casts a shadow over chip stocks\nThe semiconductor trade is losing steam following Broadcom’s earnings report\nAs Broadcom recorded the largest one-day loss of market capitalization in its history Thursday, Micron Technology did the same.\nWhile Broadcom’s earnings results Wednesday struck D.A. Davidson analyst Gil Luria as “impressive,” investors took issue with various aspects of the report. That cast a shadow over the wider chip sector, according to Luria.\nAbout the Author\nHannah Pedone is a New York–based technology reporter for MarketWatch.",
